Body:
I also have the same issue and couldn't find any solution.

When using qwen2.5-coder:32b, the output is:

> opencode run "/no_think generate a todo.md file with the contents 'hello world, from qwen3' in it"
> 
> > build · qwen2.5-coder:32b
> 
> write: {"content": "hello world, from qwen3", "filePath": "/tmp/test/todo.md"}

And no file is written.

With Gemma4, the same works nicely:

> opencode run "/no_think generate a todo.md file with the contents 'hello world, from gemma' in it"
> 
> > build · gemma4:31b
> 
> ✱ Glob "todo.md" 0 matches
> 
> ← Write todo.md
> Wrote file successfully.
> 
> Done.


My opencode.json looks like this (with the line `"model": "ollama/qwen2.5-coder:32b",` being changed when gemma4 is used):

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "ollama/qwen2.5-coder:32b",
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "models": {
        "qwen2.5-coder:32b": {
          "name": "qwen2.5-coder"
        },
        "gemma4:31b": {
          "_launch": true,
          "name": "gemma4"
        }
      },
      "name": "ollama",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://172.17.0.1:11434/v1",
        "apiKey": "anything"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I used 1.18.4 and ollama 0.32.1, so everything should be up to date. If there is any workaround, I'd be happy to know about this.

**EDIT** qwen3.6:27b works, since this is much newer and has comparable size, it probably makes sense to just switch to this model.
